Subject: [PATCH] qpnp-smbcharger: do not wait for hvdcp_opti on a cable insertion

ASUS' handle_usb_insertion() sets every insertion aside until Qualcomm's hvdcp_opti
has said that Quick Charge 3 is supported (POWER_SUPPLY_DP_DM_HVDCP3_SUPPORTED), and
retries it a second later up to twenty times. The retry runs update_usb_status(),
which calls the insertion again only for a cable present at power-on: a cable
plugged in later is set aside once and never handled, so no charging and no USB.
On stock hvdcp_opti made that announcement within seconds of every start, so nobody
saw it. In the first LineageOS 20 builds the daemon was not shipped, and nothing
made it.

Without the wait the insertion is handled at once, whether hvdcp_opti has started
yet or runs at all. The announcement still comes from the daemon when it does, and
the daemon then steps a Quick Charge 3 adapter up; the driver's other uses of the
flag are untouched.
---
--- drivers/power/qpnp-smbcharger.c
+++ drivers/power/qpnp-smbcharger.c
@@ -5911,11 +5911,6 @@
 		ret.intval = 1;
 		chip->batt_psy.set_property(&chip->batt_psy,POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ALLOW_HVDCP3, &ret);
 	}
-	if (!chip->hvdcp3_supported && support_cnt < 20){
-		queue_delayed_work(adapter_wq ,&chip_fg->usb_insertion_work, msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
-		support_cnt ++;
-		return;		
-	}
 	g_cable_poweron = false;
 	complete_all(&chip->sdp_retry_complete_flag);
 	pr_smb(PR_STATUS, "complete_all sdp_retry_complete_flag\n");
